      <problem>
        <paragraph>$${\int\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}}dx$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$- 1 + x 2 x + arcsinh x + C - 1 + x 2 x + arcsinh x + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Use the technique of completing the square to evaluate the following integrals.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="160" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}}{x^{2}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="161" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int\frac{dx}{1 - x^{2}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$- 1 1 + x + C - 1 1 + x + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="162" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{\sqrt{1 + x^{2}}}{x^{2}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="163" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{1}{x^{2} - 6x}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$arcsin x - 5 5 + C arcsin x - 5 5 + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="164" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{1}{x^{2} + 2x + 1}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="165" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Evaluate the integral without using calculus: $$\int{\frac{1}{\sqrt{-x^{2} + 2x + 8}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$9\pi 2;9\pi 2;$$ area of a semicircle with radius 3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="166" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the area enclosed by the ellipse $$\int{\frac{1}{\sqrt{-x^{2} + 10x}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="167" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Evaluate the integral $${\int\frac{1}{\sqrt{x^{2} + 4x - 12}}}dx$$ using two different substitutions. First, let $$\int_{-3}^{3}{\sqrt{9 - x^{2}} dx.}$$ and evaluate using trigonometric substitution. Second, let $$\frac{x^{2}}{4} + \frac{y^{2}}{9} = 1.$$ and use trigonometric substitution. Are the answers the same?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$arcsin(x)+Carcsin(x)+C$$ is the common answer.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="168" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Evaluate the integral $$\int\frac{dx}{\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}$$ using the substitution $$x = \cos \theta$$ Next, evaluate the same integral using the substitution $$x = \sin \theta$$ Show that the results are equivalent.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="169" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Evaluate the integral $$\int\frac{dx}{x\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}}$$ using the form $$x = \sec \theta.$$ Next, evaluate the same integral using $$x = \csc \theta.$$ Are the results the same?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$12ln(1+x2)+C12ln(1+x2)+C$$ is the result using either method.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="170" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>State the method of integration you would use to evaluate the integral $${\int\frac{x}{x^{2} + 1}}dx$$ Why did you choose this method?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="171" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>State the method of integration you would use to evaluate the integral $${\int{\frac{1}{u}du}}.$$ Why did you choose this method?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Use trigonometric substitution. Let $$x=sec(\theta ).x=sec(\theta ).$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="172" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Evaluate $$x = \tan \theta.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="173" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the length of the arc of the curve over the specified interval: $${\int{x\sqrt{x^{2} + 1} dx}}.$$ Round the answer to three decimal places.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>4.367</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="174" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the surface area of the solid generated by revolving the region bounded by the graphs of $${\int{x^{2}\sqrt{x^{2} - 1} dx}}.$$ about the x-axis. (Round the answer to three decimal places).</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="175" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>The region bounded by the graph of $$\int_{-1}^{1}\frac{x dx}{x^{2} + 1}$$ and the x-axis between $$y = \ln x,\lbrack 1,5\rbrack.$$ and $$y = x^{2},y = 0,x = 0, \text{and} x = \sqrt{2}$$ is revolved about the x-axis. Find the volume of the solid that is generated.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$\pi 2 8 + \pi 4 \pi 2 8 + \pi 4$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Solve the initial-value problem for y as a function of x.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="176" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = \frac{1}{1 + x^{2}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="177" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y = 1 16 ln | x + 8 x - 8 | + 3 y = 1 16 ln | x + 8 x - 8 | + 3$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="178" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the area bounded by $$x = 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="179" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>An oil storage tank can be described as the volume generated by revolving the area bounded by $$\left( {x^{2} + 36} \right)\frac{dy}{dx} = 1,y(6) = 0$$ about the x-axis. Find the volume of the tank (in cubic meters).</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>24.6 m3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="180" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>During each cycle, the velocity v (in feet per second) of a robotic welding device is given by $$\left( {64 - x^{2}} \right)\frac{dy}{dx} = 1,y(0) = 3$$ where t is time in seconds. Find the expression for the displacement s (in feet) as a function of t if $$y = \frac{2}{\sqrt{64 - 4x^{2}}},x = 0,y = 0, \text{and} x = 2.$$ when $$y = \frac{16}{\sqrt{64 + x^{2}}},x = 0,y = 0,x = 2$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="181" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the length of the curve $$v = 2t - \frac{14}{4 + t^{2}},$$ between $$s = 0$$ and $$t = 0.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 \pi 3 2 \pi 3$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
